---
import "../sternzeit/sternzeit.css";
import "./helldunkel.css";

const WHITES = [
    ["D65", "D65, noon daylight, about 6500 K: the white of sRGB, Display P3 and Rec. 2020"],
    ["D50", "D50, warmer daylight, about 5000 K: the white of print"],
    ["A", "Illuminant A, an incandescent lamp, about 2856 K"],
];
---

<figure class="scene-frame" id="chromaticity">
    <div class="chromaticity" data-field="plot">
        <canvas data-field="canvas" aria-label="The colors a screen shows within the CIE 1931 chromaticity diagram"></canvas>
        <div data-field="overlay"></div>
    </div>
    <p class="hdri-controls">
        <span class="steps" role="radiogroup" aria-label="White point">
            <span class="steps-heading" aria-hidden="true">white point</span>
            {WHITES.map(([value, title]) => (
                <label title={title}>
                    <input type="radio" name="chromaticity-white" value={value} checked={value === "D65"} />
                    <span>{value}</span>
                </label>
            ))}
        </span>
        <span class="steps" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Which colors are filled in">
            <span class="steps-heading" aria-hidden="true">colors</span>
            {["sRGB", "P3"].map((value) => (
                <label>
                    <input type="radio" name="chromaticity-fill" value={value} checked={value === "sRGB"} />
                    <span>{value}</span>
                </label>
            ))}
        </span>
        <span class="chromaticity-swatch" data-field="swatch" title="This white as sRGB shows it"></span>
        <span class="note" data-field="info"></span>
    </p>
    <figcaption class="figure-caption">
        Every color the eye can tell apart, by chromaticity, the spectrum's pure colors along the curved edge, computed by
        Wyman's fit. The triangles are what three primaries can mix: sRGB, Display P3 and Rec. 2020, and the mark is the
        white point. The colors fill the triangle chosen, P3 only on a screen that shows it, and outside it there is nothing a screen could show right.
    </figcaption>
</figure>

<script>
    import "./chromaticity";
</script>
